hcare decision systems, applied ML research, and analytics impact."}],["$","meta","14",{"name":"twitter:image","content":"https://anuraagbhavaraju.github.io/og.png"}],["$","link","15",{"rel":"shortcut icon","href":"https://anuraagbhavaraju.github.io/favicon.svg"}],["$","link","16",{"rel":"icon","href":"https://anuraagbhavaraju.github.io/favicon.svg"}]],[["$","meta","0",{"name":"viewport","content":"width=device-width, initial-scale=1"}]]],["$","$L3",null,{"segmentMap":{"children":["case-studies","customer-cosmos"]},"children":["$","$L4",null,{"id":"layout:/","parallelSlots":"$undefined","children":["$","$L5",null,{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"segmentMap":{"children":[]},"children":["$","$L4",null,{"id":"page:/case-studies/customer-cosmos/"}]}]}]}]}]],"__layoutFlags":{"layout:/":"s"},"__artifactCompatibility":{"schemaVersion":1,"graphVersion":"app-route-graph:16e2pkfyc4ff4","deploymentVersion":"8c101f9c-ae08-4053-9d81-570cfe80a1ab","appElementsSchemaVersion":1,"rscPayloadSchemaVersion":1,"rootBoundaryId":"/","renderEpoch":null}}
1:["$","main",null,{"className":"case-study-main","children":[["$","nav",null,{"className":"case-nav","aria-label":"Case study navigation","children":[["$","a",null,{"className":"brand-mark","href":"/","aria-label":"Anuraag Bhavaraju home","children":"AB"}],["$","a",null,{"className":"button secondary-button","href":"/#work","children":"Back To Portfolio"}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"case-study-article","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"case-hero","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"section-kicker","children":"Selected Work"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"case-eyebrow","children":["Customer Intelligence"," - ","3-5 min read"]}],["$","h1",null,{"children":"Customer Cosmos"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"A customer intelligence accelerator that harmonizes fragmented omnichannel data into a customer 360 layer for personalization, activation, marketing optimization, and customer lifetime value decisions."}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"case-stats","aria-label":"Key proof points","children":[["$","div","$$3B+ marketing spend optimized",{"children":"$$3B+ marketing spend optimized"}],["$","div","25M+ at-risk customers re-engaged",{"children":"25M+ at-risk customers re-engaged"}],["$","div","$$300 nearly increased customer lifetime value per household",{"children":"$$300 nearly increased customer lifetime value per household"}],["$","div","200+ customer attributes powering intelligence",{"children":"200+ customer attributes powering intelligence"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"case-body","children":[["$","aside",null,{"className":"case-sidebar","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"section-kicker","children":"Methods"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"tag-row","children":[["$","span","Customer 360",{"children":"Customer 360"}],["$","span","CLTV",{"children":"CLTV"}],["$","span","Propensity models",{"children":"Propensity models"}],["$","span","Feature stores",{"children":"Feature stores"}],["$","span","CX personalization",{"children":"CX personalization"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"section-kicker","children":"Further Reading"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"source-list","children":[["$","li","https://www.tredence.com/solutions/customer-cosmos",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"https://www.tredence.com/solutions/customer-cosmos","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":"Tredence Customer Cosmos solution page"}]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"case-sections","children":[["$","section","The Problem",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"The Problem"}],[["$","p","Most large consumer businesses have more customer data than they can actually use. The issue is fragmentation: transaction data in one system, loyalty data in another, digital behavior elsewhere, campaign response data in yet another layer, and limited visibility into what customers do outside the brand's own ecosystem. This makes personalization slow, segmentation shallow, and marketing optimization dependent on partial signals.",{"children":"Most large consumer businesses have more customer data than they can actually use. The issue is fragmentation: transaction data in one system, loyalty data in another, digital behavior elsewhere, campaign response data in yet another layer, and limited visibility into what customers do outside the brand's own ecosystem. This makes personalization slow, segmentation shallow, and marketing optimization dependent on partial signals."}],["$","p","Tredence describes Customer Cosmos as an end-to-end customer intelligence solution built to harmonize siloed omnichannel data, enrich customer insights, and create rest-of-market visibility. That framing is important: the problem is not only reporting. It is turning scattered customer data into a decision layer that can power growth, retention, monetization, and activation.",{"children":"Tredence describes Customer Cosmos as an end-to-end customer intelligence solution built to harmonize siloed omnichannel data, enrich customer insights, and create rest-of-market visibility. That framing is important: the problem is not only reporting. It is turning scattered customer data into a decision layer that can power growth, retention, monetization, and activation."}]]]}],"$L6","$L7"]}]]}]]}]]}]
6:["$","section","The Product Logic",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"The Product Logic"}],[["$","p","Customer Cosmos creates a unified customer view across first-party omnichannel sources and enriches it with external data partnerships. The public solution page describes a comprehensive feature store with 200+ attributes, including signals such as recency, subscription, app download, tenure, clickstream behavior, and more. On top of that feature layer, the solution supports models for propensity, customer lifetime value, headroom, and price sensitivity.",{"children":"Customer Cosmos creates a unified customer view across first-party omnichannel sources and enriches it with external data partnerships. The public solution page describes a comprehensive feature store with 200+ attributes, including signals such as recency, subscription, app download, tenure, clickstream behavior, and more. On top of that feature layer, the solution supports models for propensity, customer lifetime value, headroom, and price sensitivity."}],["$","p","The strongest part of the case is the movement from data foundation to business activation. A customer 360 layer becomes valuable only when it is used by downstream teams: marketing, merchandising, digital, loyalty, store innovation, supplier monetization, and executive decision-making. Customer Cosmos links analytics to activation through reporting, segmentation, next-best-experience logic, and customer intelligence applications.",{"children":"The strongest part of the case is the movement from data foundation to business activation. A customer 360 layer becomes valuable only when it is used by downstream teams: marketing, merchandising, digital, loyalty, store innovation, supplier monetization, and executive decision-making. Customer Cosmos links analytics to activation through reporting, segmentation, next-best-experience logic, and customer intelligence applications."}]]]}]
7:["$","section","How I Worked On It",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"How I Worked On It"}],[["$","p","I worked on Customer Cosmos as a senior data science delivery problem, not as a one-off modelling exercise. The work meant leading data scientists through client implementations where the same accelerator had to adapt to different customer data realities, commercial priorities, and activation channels. The technical surface included segmentation, propensity modelling, customer lifetime value estimation, marketing analytics, and reusable delivery assets that made implementations faster and more consistent.",{"children":"I worked on Customer Cosmos as a senior data science delivery problem, not as a one-off modelling exercise. The work meant leading data scientists through client implementations where the same accelerator had to adapt to different customer data realities, commercial priorities, and activation channels. The technical surface included segmentation, propensity modelling, customer lifetime value estimation, marketing analytics, and reusable delivery assets that made implementations faster and more consistent."}],["$","p","What I like about this work is that the ML is tied very directly to decisions. A propensity score, CLTV estimate, or customer attribute is only useful if a marketer, category lead, loyalty team, or executive can act on it. Customer Cosmos connected those model outputs to the operating questions businesses actually ask: who is at risk, who has room to grow, what message should go next, and where marketing spend is being wasted.",{"children":"What I like about this work is that the ML is tied very directly to decisions. A propensity score, CLTV estimate, or customer attribute is only useful if a marketer, category lead, loyalty team, or executive can act on it. Customer Cosmos connected those model outputs to the operating questions businesses actually ask: who is at risk, who has room to grow, what message should go next, and where marketing spend is being wasted."}],["$","p","The scale is the proof point. The public solution page reports over $3B in marketing spend optimized, 25M+ at-risk customers re-engaged, and nearly $300 increase in customer lifetime value per household. For me, that makes it a strong example of enterprise ML working as a decision layer rather than a dashboard parked on the side.",{"children":"The scale is the proof point. The public solution page reports over $3B in marketing spend optimized, 25M+ at-risk customers re-engaged, and nearly $300 increase in customer lifetime value per household. For me, that makes it a strong example of enterprise ML working as a decision layer rather than a dashboard parked on the side."}]]]}]
